<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Aurora Goods Analytics</title>
<meta name="description" content="Executive analytics dashboard for Aurora Goods Co. (fictional), generated by retail-analytics-lakehouse.">
<style>
  :root {
    --page: #f9f9f7; --surface: #fcfcfb; --ink: #0b0b0b; --ink-2: #52514e; --muted: #898781;
    --grid: #e1e0d9; --border: rgba(11,11,11,0.10); --accent: #2a78d6; --good: #006300; --bad: #d03b3b;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--page); color: var(--ink);
         font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; line-height: 1.5; }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
  header { background: #0d366b; color: #fff; padding: 32px 16px 28px; }
  .wrap { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 16px; }
  header .wrap { padding: 0; }
  header h1 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 28px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  header p { margin: 0; color: #cde2fb; font-size: 14px; }
  nav { margin-top: 16px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 16px; font-size: 14px; }
  nav a { color: #fff; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.35); }
  main { padding: 24px 0 48px; }
  section { margin-top: 32px; }
  h2 { font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .lede { color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0 0 16px; font-size: 14px; max-width: 820px; }
  .kpis { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(170px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
  .kpi { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; }
  .kpi .label { font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-2); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  .kpi .value { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 650; margin-top: 2px; }
  .kpi .delta { font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-2); margin-top: 2px; }
  .kpi .delta .up { color: var(--good); font-weight: 600; }
  .kpi .delta .down { color: var(--bad); font-weight: 600; }
  .grid2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 480px), 1fr)); gap: 16px; }
  .card { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px;
          padding: 16px 16px 8px; margin-top: 16px; min-width: 0; }
  .grid2 .card { margin-top: 0; }
  .card h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; }
  .card .sub { margin: 2px 0 8px; font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-2); }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 13px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--grid); }
  th { color: var(--ink-2); font-weight: 600; }
  td.n, th.n { text-align: right; }
  .table-wrap { overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .insights { counter-reset: ins; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;
              display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 360px), 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
  .insights li { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 16px; }
  .insights .area { font-size: 11px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
  .insights .head { font-weight: 650; margin: 2px 0 6px; }
  .insights .detail { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0; }
  .pill { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600;
          border: 1px solid var(--border); background: #fff; }
  .pill.pass::before { content: "\2713  "; color: var(--good); }
  .pill.warn::before { content: "!  "; color: #b07800; }
  .pill.fail::before { content: "\2715  "; color: var(--bad); }
  footer { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; padding: 24px 0 40px; border-top: 1px solid var(--grid); }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { header h1 { font-size: 22px; } .kpi .value { font-size: 22px; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Aurora Goods Co. &mdash; Executive Analytics</h1>
    <p>Fictional direct-to-consumer retailer &middot; {{ period }} &middot; as of {{ as_of }} &middot;
       generated {{ generated }} by <a href="{{ repo_url }}" style="color:#fff">retail-analytics-lakehouse</a></p>
    <nav>
      <a href="#kpis">KPIs</a><a href="#revenue">Revenue</a><a href="#customers">Customers</a>
      <a href="#marketing">Marketing &amp; funnel</a><a href="#merch">Merchandising</a>
      <a href="#clv">CLV model</a><a href="#insights">Insights</a><a href="#quality">Data quality &amp; pipeline</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>
<main class="wrap">

<section id="kpis">
  <h2>Headline KPIs</h2>
  <p class="lede">All revenue figures are net of discounts, exclude shipping and cancelled orders. Year-over-year compares the last 12 months with the 12 months before.</p>
  <div class="kpis">
  {% for k in kpis %}
    <div class="kpi"><div class="label">{{ k.label }}</div><div class="value">{{ k.value }}</div>
      <div class="delta">{% if k.delta %}<span class="{{ k.delta_class }}">{{ k.delta }}</span> {% endif %}{{ k.note }}</div></div>
  {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="revenue">
  <h2>Revenue &amp; seasonality</h2>
  <p class="lede">Weekly rhythm, annual seasonality, promotions and Black Friday / Cyber Monday peaks, on a customer base that compounds month over month.</p>
  <div class="card"><h3>Net revenue per day</h3><p class="sub">Thin line = daily; bold line = 7-day average. Hover for values.</p>{{ fig.revenue_trend }}</div>
  <div class="grid2" style="margin-top:16px">
    <div class="card"><h3>Monthly net revenue</h3><p class="sub">Hover for orders and new customers.</p>{{ fig.monthly }}</div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Average net revenue by weekday</h3><p class="sub">Sunday is the peak shopping day.</p>{{ fig.weekday }}</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="customers">
  <h2>Customers: retention, RFM and lifetime value</h2>
  <p class="lede">Monthly acquisition cohorts, RFM segmentation and model-based 12-month customer lifetime value.</p>
  <div class="card"><h3>Cohort retention</h3><p class="sub">Share of each first-order cohort that orders again n months later (complete months only; colour scale capped at 30%).</p>{{ fig.cohort }}</div>
  <div class="grid2" style="margin-top:16px">
    <div class="card"><h3>RFM segments</h3><p class="sub">Share of purchasing customers vs share of revenue.</p>{{ fig.rfm }}</div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Predicted 12-month CLV by RFM segment</h3><p class="sub">BG/NBD x Gamma-Gamma x margin rate (gross margin, USD).</p>{{ fig.clv_segment }}</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="marketing">
  <h2>Marketing &amp; funnel</h2>
  <p class="lede">Last-touch attribution: each order is credited to the traffic source of the session containing its purchase event.</p>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card"><h3>Return on ad spend</h3><p class="sub">Attributed net revenue / spend per paid channel (log scale).</p>{{ fig.roas }}</div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Funnel by device</h3><p class="sub">Share of sessions reaching each step.</p>{{ fig.funnel }}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="card"><h3>Channel table</h3><p class="sub">Paid channels carry spend; organic/owned channels are shown for completeness.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table>
      <tr><th>Channel</th><th>Type</th><th class="n">Spend</th><th class="n">Orders</th><th class="n">Attributed revenue</th><th class="n">ROAS</th><th class="n">POAS</th><th class="n">New customers</th><th class="n">CAC</th></tr>
      {% for r in channel_rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.channel }}</td><td>{{ r.type }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.spend }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.orders }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.revenue }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.roas }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.poas }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.new_customers }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.cac }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="merch">
  <h2>Merchandising</h2>
  <p class="lede">Which products are bought together, and where returns concentrate.</p>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card"><h3>Top product pairs by lift</h3><p class="sub">Pairs above the minimum-support threshold; hover for confidence and order counts.</p>{{ fig.pairs }}</div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Returns by category</h3><p class="sub">Returned units / units sold, with the most common reason.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap"><table>
        <tr><th>Category</th><th class="n">Units sold</th><th class="n">Returned</th><th class="n">Return rate</th><th>Top reason</th></tr>
        {% for r in return_rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.category }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.units }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.returned }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.rate }}</td><td>{{ r.reason }}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </table></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="clv">
  <h2>CLV model validation</h2>
  <p class="lede">{{ clv_text }}</p>
  <div class="card"><h3>Backtest: forecast vs actual purchases in a 26-week holdout</h3><p class="sub">Customers grouped by repeat purchases during calibration.</p>{{ fig.backtest }}</div>
</section>

<section id="insights">
  <h2>Insights</h2>
  <p class="lede">Generated automatically from this run's gold tables (also in <code>docs/insights.md</code>).</p>
  <ol class="insights">
  {% for ins in insights %}
    <li><div class="area">{{ ins.area }}</div><div class="head">{{ ins.headline }}</div><p class="detail">{{ ins.detail }}</p></li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ol>
</section>

<section id="quality">
  <h2>Data quality &amp; pipeline</h2>
  <p class="lede">{{ dq_text }}</p>
  <div class="card"><h3>Data-quality tests by layer</h3><p class="sub">Bronze warnings document problems in the landing zone; silver and gold tests are the contract (error severity fails the run).</p>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table>
      <tr><th>Layer</th><th class="n">Tests</th><th class="n">Pass</th><th class="n">Warn</th><th class="n">Fail</th></tr>
      {% for r in dq_rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.layer }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.total }}</td><td class="n"><span class="pill pass">{{ r.pass }}</span></td><td class="n"><span class="pill warn">{{ r.warn }}</span></td><td class="n"><span class="pill fail">{{ r.fail }}</span></td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table></div>
  </div>
  <div class="grid2" style="margin-top:16px">
    <div class="card"><h3>Quarantined rows by reason</h3><p class="sub">Rejected by silver models, kept in <code>quarantine.*</code> tables with a rejection_reason.</p>{{ fig.quarantine }}</div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Model run times</h3><p class="sub">Slowest models of the latest DAG run (DuckDB, {{ threads }} threads).</p>{{ fig.timings }}</div>
  </div>
  {% if pipeline_rows %}
  <div class="card"><h3>Pipeline steps (latest run-all)</h3><p class="sub">Wall time and peak resident memory (process + worker children) per step on {{ hardware }}.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table>
      <tr><th>Step</th><th class="n">Wall time</th><th class="n">Peak RSS</th></tr>
      {% for r in pipeline_rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.step }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.seconds }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.rss }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table></div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if storage_rows %}
  <div class="card"><h3>Storage footprint</h3><p class="sub">Raw CSV / JSON Lines vs zstd Parquet (bronze) vs the DuckDB warehouse (silver + gold + quarantine + meta).</p>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table>
      <tr><th>Layer</th><th class="n">Size</th></tr>
      {% for r in storage_rows %}<tr><td>{{ r.layer }}</td><td class="n">{{ r.size }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
    </table></div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
</section>
</main>
<footer class="wrap">
  Aurora Goods Co. is fictional and every record is synthetic. Built with DuckDB, Parquet and Plotly.
  Source: <a href="{{ repo_url }}">{{ repo_url }}</a>.
</footer>
</body>
</html>
